Host keys and power or rocker presses that don't fit the Dana's 32-report keyboard FIFO wait in order in a saved backlog of up to 8192 changes, fed into the FIFO as the guest reads reports and from CycleSlowly. While the ST is halted the waiting keys stay for after the wake; only a key that wakes it goes in, with its release. Presses past the limit are refused, and a refused power or rocker press is logged instead of thrown. The ST chunk is variable length from v11, so words left after its backlog are accepted. A key pressed again now waits 200 ms after its release instead of 100, as the ROM can take a press about 100 ms after the release twice.

